// Generated by nsx_add_segger_targets() via configure_file(@ONLY).
// Standard SEGGER J-Link Commander script: halt, load the built .bin at the
// board's flash/MRAM origin (NSX_SEGGER_PF_ADDR, e.g. Apollo510's MCU_MRAM
// ORIGIN 0x00410000 per modules/nsx-ambiq-sdk .../apollo510/gcc/linker_script_sbl.ld),
// then reset and run.
//
// CONFIRMED (2026-08-05): this r/h/loadbin/r/g/qc sequence, the
// 0x00410000 load address, and device=AP510NFA-CBR/if=SWD/speed=4000
// (passed as -device/-if/-speed CLI args by nsx_add_segger_targets() in
// cmake/nsx/nsx_helpers.cmake, equivalent to `device`/`si`/`speed` in-file
// commands) match the known-working JLink invocation for Apollo510.
//
// NOTE: on parts that require a signed/SBL-wrapped image (Apollo5-series
// commonly does), loading a raw .bin at this address may not be sufficient
// for a production boot path -- verify against Ambiq's official flashing
// flow before relying on this for anything beyond development/debug use
// with SBL configured to accept unsigned images.
r
h
loadbin "@NSX_JLINK_BIN_FILE@", @NSX_SEGGER_PF_ADDR@
r
g
qc
